From 4e367338a68cb5328213484ecd1b7e201b2de339 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Galih Tama <galpt@v.recipes>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 18:26:14 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 30/40] v4.8-gpu: clear the wakeup flags on the throttled
 enqueue path

A wakeup that lands on a throttled cfs_rq returns early from
enqueue_task_fair() before place_entity() runs, so futex_waiting and
ipc_waiting were left set for the whole throttle duration and could
produce a stale vslice boost when the task was finally unthrottled.
Clear both flags on the throttled path so a boost is only ever granted by
an actual place_entity() wakeup.

Signed-off-by: Galih Tama <galpt@v.recipes>
---
 kernel/sched/fair.c | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/kernel/sched/fair.c b/kernel/sched/fair.c
index dd6924ed6..d88ad9417 100644
--- a/kernel/sched/fair.c
+++ b/kernel/sched/fair.c
@@ -8303,8 +8303,15 @@ enqueue_task_fair(struct rq *rq, struct task_struct *p, int flags)
 	unsigned long weight;
 	bool curr;
 
-	if (task_is_throttled(p) && enqueue_throttled_task(p))
+	if (task_is_throttled(p) && enqueue_throttled_task(p)) {
+		/* A wakeup that lands on a throttled cfs_rq does not reach
+		 * place_entity(); clear the wake flags so they cannot produce
+		 * a stale boost when the task is unthrottled later.
+		 */
+		WRITE_ONCE(p->infinity.futex_waiting, false);
+		WRITE_ONCE(p->infinity.ipc_waiting, false);
 		return;
+	}
 
